// The allocator library: owned memory, byte buffers, formatting and
// collections.
// Needs `malloc`/`realloc`/`free`/`abort`, from libc or the program.
//
// Running out of memory aborts the program: every constructor and every
// operation that grows a container (`Buffer!::new`, `push`, `insert`, the
// arenas, ...) stops it with `abort` when `malloc` or `realloc` fails, and
// none of them returns an error for it. A program that can recover makes
// its containers with the fallible constructors, which return
// `heap::AllocError` instead: `heap::Storage::try_alloc`/`try_grow`,
// `owned::Owned!::try_new`, `buffer::Buffer!::try_new_with_cap`,
// `collections::vec::Vec!::try_new` and `OwnedVec!::try_new`, and
// `collections::hashmap::HashMap!::try_new` and `OwnedMap!::try_new`. A
// container made so still aborts if it later fails to grow.
use package::{arena, buffer, collections, fmt, heap, owned};
export arena;
export buffer;
export collections;
export fmt;
export heap;
export owned;
